[ti:How Spyre Became a Native PyTorch Device]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: If an accelerator runs PyTorch models, why should we care whether PyTorch sees it as a real device?
[00:00.00]Ava：如果加速器能运行 PyTorch 模型，为什么还要在意 PyTorch 是否把它识别为真正的设备？
[00:07.55]Brian: Because that decides whether tensors can stay on it between operations.
[00:07.55]Brian：因为这决定了张量能否在操作之间留在加速器上。
[00:12.67]For IBM's Spyre accelerator, native device support also cuts launch work and lets data movement overlap computation.
[00:12.67]对 IBM 的 Spyre 加速器来说，原生设备支持还能减少启动开销，让数据传输与计算重叠。
[00:21.39]Ava: So this is about more than making one model compile?
[00:21.39]Ava：所以这不只是让一个模型编译成功？
[00:25.17]Brian: Exactly. Spyre is a dataflow AI accelerator optimized for inference.
[00:25.17]Brian：没错。Spyre 是专为推理优化的数据流 AI 加速器。
[00:30.36]The goal is familiar PyTorch code, with the storage and scheduling behavior the hardware needs.
[00:30.36]目标是让开发者照常编写 PyTorch 代码，同时满足硬件对存储和调度的要求。
[00:37.95]Ava: Let's start with the hardware. What does dataflow mean here?
[00:37.95]Ava：先说硬件。这里的“数据流”是什么意思？
[00:42.14]Brian: A compiled Spyre kernel contains programs for several kinds of functional unit.
[00:42.14]Brian：编译后的 Spyre 内核包含面向多种功能单元的程序。
[00:47.73]Those units make progress when their input data arrives.
[00:47.73]这些单元在收到输入数据后就开始工作。
[00:51.68]Think of stations in a workshop: each starts its part when the previous station delivers the pieces.
[00:51.68]可以把它想成车间里的工位：上一个工位送来零件，下一个工位就开始干活。
[00:59.10]Ava: And the compiler decides how those stations work together?
[00:59.10]Ava：编译器负责决定这些工位如何配合？
[01:03.51]Brian: Right.
[01:03.51]Brian：对。
[01:03.93]It builds the device-side schedule, including movement between large device memory and each core's local scratchpad.
[01:03.93]它会生成设备端的调度安排，包括大容量设备内存与各核心本地暂存区之间的数据传输。
[01:12.21]The runtime submits the compiled program and its tensor arguments.
[01:12.21]运行时负责提交编译后的程序及其张量参数。
[01:17.27]Ava: Can the runtime launch two compute jobs at once to keep the card busy?
[01:17.27]Ava：运行时能同时启动两个计算任务，让加速卡保持忙碌吗？
[01:22.52]Brian: Independently submitted compute jobs share one runtime compute queue.
[01:22.52]Brian：独立提交的计算任务共用一个运行时计算队列。
[01:27.60]They wait behind each other.
[01:27.60]它们得排队执行。
[01:29.66]But transfers have separate pipelines, so data can move while a program computes.
[01:29.66]但数据传输有独立的流水线，因此程序计算时也能传输数据。
[01:35.97]Ava: Got it. The useful overlap is transfer with compute. How does PyTorch express that?
[01:35.97]Ava：明白了，能重叠的是传输和计算。PyTorch 怎么表达这一点？
[01:43.23]Brian: With streams: ordered queues of work.
[01:43.23]Brian：通过流，也就是按顺序执行任务的队列。
[01:46.21]PyTorch also has events, which let one stream wait for work on another.
[01:46.21]PyTorch 还有事件，可以让一个流等待另一个流上的任务。
[01:51.91]torch-spyre maps those ideas onto Spyre's runtime.
[01:51.91]torch-spyre 把这些概念映射到 Spyre 的运行时。
[01:56.28]Ava: Before streams, though, PyTorch needs to recognize Spyre.
[01:56.28]Ava：不过在用流之前，PyTorch 得先识别 Spyre。
[02:01.09]What gives it a device identity?
[02:01.09]是什么赋予它设备身份的？
[02:04.14]Brian: PrivateUse1, PyTorch's extension slot for an outside device backend.
[02:04.14]Brian：PrivateUse1，这是 PyTorch 为外部设备后端预留的扩展槽位。
[02:09.36]torch-spyre names that slot spyre and registers a device module.
[02:09.36]torch-spyre 把这个槽位命名为 spyre，并注册设备模块。
[02:14.27]With allocator, copy, and dispatcher support, a tensor can move to Spyre and operations can reach Spyre kernels.
[02:14.27]有了分配器、拷贝和分发器支持，张量就能移到 Spyre 上，操作也能调用 Spyre 内核。
[02:23.21]Ava: Does that also explain why ordinary PyTorch streams can work?
[02:23.21]Ava：这也解释了为什么普通的 PyTorch 流能用吗？
[02:28.24]Brian: Yes. The backend implements the device-guard hooks PyTorch asks for.
[02:28.24]Brian：是的。后端实现了 PyTorch 所需的设备守卫钩子。
[02:33.49]Then native stream creation and stream selection use PyTorch's own interface.
[02:33.49]之后就能通过 PyTorch 自己的接口创建和选择原生流。
[02:39.78]Ava: Let's talk about tensors staying put. What went wrong with the earlier approach?
[02:39.78]Ava：再说说张量留在设备上。之前的做法有什么问题？
[02:45.24]Brian: The earlier custom compiler backend could keep selected model state on Spyre through special runtime paths.
[02:45.24]Brian：之前的自定义编译器后端能通过特殊的运行时路径，把部分模型状态保留在 Spyre 上。
[02:52.72]But PyTorch still saw ordinary tensors as CPU tensors, even when the runtime had moved their data.
[02:52.72]但在 PyTorch 看来，普通张量仍是 CPU 张量，即使运行时已经搬走了它们的数据。
[02:59.92]Ava: That sounds expensive for eager execution, where operations happen one at a time.
[02:59.92]Ava：对逐个执行操作的即时执行模式来说，听起来开销很大。
[03:06.53]Brian: It was a poor fit. Each small operation could become another transfer boundary.
[03:06.53]Brian：确实不合适。每个小操作都可能产生一次额外的数据传输。
[03:12.20]A native Spyre tensor instead has device storage managed through PyTorch's allocator and storage lifetime.
[03:12.20]原生 Spyre 张量则使用设备存储，由 PyTorch 的分配器管理内存及其生命周期。
[03:20.15]Ava: So PyTorch knows the tensor is resident, and it knows when to release its memory?
[03:20.15]Ava：所以 PyTorch 知道张量留在设备上，也知道何时释放内存？
[03:26.57]Brian: Exactly.
[03:26.57]Brian：正是。
[03:27.17]When the last reference goes away, PyTorch calls the backend allocator to release or recycle the allocation.
[03:27.17]最后一个引用消失时，PyTorch 会调用后端分配器，释放或回收那块内存。
[03:35.54]Ava: Is Spyre memory just one big set of pointers?
[03:35.54]Ava：Spyre 内存就是一大堆指针吗？
[03:39.42]Brian: Underneath the allocator interface, memory comes in regions, each with a handle.
[03:39.42]Brian：在分配器接口之下，内存按区域划分，每个区域都有一个句柄。
[03:45.29]The allocator takes a small number of large regions and divides them into aligned blocks.
[03:45.29]分配器取少量大内存区域，将其切分为对齐的内存块。
[03:51.82]Many tensors can then share a few handles.
[03:51.82]这样，许多张量就能共用少数几个句柄。
[03:55.25]Ava: Why keep the number of handles low?
[03:55.25]Ava：为什么要尽量少用句柄？
[03:58.00]Brian: The handle budget is limited, especially when tenants share a card.
[03:58.00]Brian：句柄数量有限，尤其是在多个租户共用一张卡时。
[04:03.20]An allocation is described by a region, an offset, and a length.
[04:03.20]一块分配的内存由区域、偏移量和长度来描述。
[04:08.18]A tensor spread across memory domains may need several such pieces.
[04:08.18]如果张量分布在多个内存域，就可能需要好几个这样的片段。
[04:13.73]Ava: Memory domains? Are we talking about several cards?
[04:13.73]Ava：内存域？是说有好几张卡吗？
[04:18.45]Brian: No, locality within one device.
[04:18.45]Brian：不是，是同一设备内的局部性。
[04:20.73]Some cores reach certain memory domains more efficiently.
[04:20.73]有些核心访问特定内存域时效率更高。
[04:24.93]A tensor can sit near the cores using it or be spread across domains for bandwidth.
[04:24.93]张量可以放在使用它的计算核心附近，也可以分布在多个域中以提高带宽。
[04:31.04]That placement matters because compiled code may depend on it.
[04:31.04]放在哪里很重要，因为编译后的代码可能依赖这个位置。
[04:35.96]Ava: And layout matters too, I assume?
[04:35.96]Ava：布局也很重要吧？
[04:38.81]Brian: It does. Compiled kernels expect particular layouts.
[04:38.81]Brian：对。编译后的计算核要求特定的布局。
[04:42.68]Model adapters prepare weights and key-value caches, the stored attention state, in those layouts.
[04:42.68]模型适配器会按这些布局准备权重和键值缓存，也就是保存的注意力状态。
[04:49.98]Compiler passes add legal conversions for intermediate tensors.
[04:49.98]编译器的处理阶段会为中间张量加入合法的布局转换。
[04:55.02]Ava: Let me recap: PyTorch owns tensor lifetime, while the Spyre allocator describes the real device placement.
[04:55.02]Ava：我总结一下：PyTorch 管理张量的生命周期，Spyre 分配器则描述它在设备上的实际位置。
[05:03.72]Brian: That's it.
[05:03.72]Brian：没错。
[05:04.38]Now the next problem is launching a compiled program with tensors whose addresses weren't known when it was compiled.
[05:04.38]接下来的问题是：张量地址在编译时还不知道，怎样用这些张量启动编译好的程序。
[05:12.40]Ava: Why weren't they known?
[05:12.40]Ava：为什么当时不知道地址？
[05:14.62]Brian: The compiler fixes the program's layout ahead of time.
[05:14.62]Brian：编译器会提前确定程序布局。
[05:18.58]But PyTorch's allocator places caller-owned input and output tensors later.
[05:18.58]但 PyTorch 分配器要到之后才会放置调用方持有的输入和输出张量。
[05:24.08]Their addresses must stay symbolic until launch.
[05:24.08]因此，它们的地址在启动前必须保持为符号值。
[05:27.96]Ava: What did the earlier runtime do?
[05:27.96]Ava：早期的运行时怎么处理？
[05:30.71]Brian: One path copied inputs into buffers owned by the compiled job, then copied results out.
[05:30.71]Brian：一种方式是把输入复制到编译任务自己的缓冲区，再把结果复制出来。
[05:37.17]Another bound a small set of device address windows to tensors.
[05:37.17]另一种方式是把少量设备地址窗口绑定到张量。
[05:41.85]That avoided copies, but the number of windows limited how many tensor inputs a fused kernel could take.
[05:41.85]这样省去了复制，但窗口数量限制了融合计算核能接收的张量输入数。
[05:49.92]Ava: What's the current solution?
[05:49.92]Ava：现在怎么解决？
[05:52.12]Brian: Launch-time patching. The compiled binary has placeholders for tensor addresses.
[05:52.12]Brian：在启动时修补地址。编译后的二进制程序里留有张量地址占位符。
[05:58.08]At launch, a CPU callback writes the actual addresses into a pinned host buffer.
[05:58.08]启动时，CPU 回调会把实际地址写入锁页主机缓冲区。
[06:04.04]A transfer moves that correction data to the program's device allocation.
[06:04.04]然后通过传输，把这些修补数据送到程序在设备上分配的内存。
[06:09.48]Then the device uses it to patch the operands.
[06:09.48]设备再用这些数据修补操作数。
[06:13.25]Ava: Like filling in delivery addresses after the packages are packed?
[06:13.25]Ava：就像包裹打好后再填收货地址？
[06:17.30]Brian: Pretty much. The package layout is fixed; the destinations arrive later.
[06:17.30]Brian：差不多。包裹怎么装是固定的，目的地稍后才知道。
[06:22.52]Those three steps need strict ordering, or the program could read an address before it's ready.
[06:22.52]这三步必须严格按顺序执行，否则程序可能读到尚未准备好的地址。
[06:29.77]Ava: Would putting everything on one stream solve that?
[06:29.77]Ava：把所有步骤放在同一个流上能解决吗？
[06:33.48]Brian: It would preserve order, but it would also make preparation wait while compute runs.
[06:33.48]Brian：能保证顺序，但计算运行时，准备工作也得等着。
[06:39.32]The initial design uses a preparation stream for the CPU callback and transfer, and a device stream for compute.
[06:39.32]初版设计用一个准备流执行 CPU 回调和传输，另一个设备流执行计算。
[06:47.10]An event makes compute wait for its transfer.
[06:47.10]事件会让计算等待对应的传输完成。
[06:50.58]Ava: Then preparation for the next invocation can happen during the current computation?
[06:50.58]Ava：那下一次调用的准备工作就能和当前计算同时进行？
[06:56.09]Brian: Yes. Its tensor addresses are already known at launch.
[06:56.09]Brian：对。启动时，下一次调用的张量地址已经确定了。
[07:00.21]A transfer can overlap too, provided it targets device storage the current computation isn't using.
[07:00.21]传输也可以重叠进行，前提是它写入的设备存储区未被当前计算使用。
[07:08.10]Ava: What if both invocations use the same device correction area?
[07:08.10]Ava：如果两次调用都用同一块设备端修补区呢？
[07:12.51]Brian: Then the next transfer must wait until the earlier compute finishes reading that area.
[07:12.51]Brian：下一次传输就必须等前一次计算读完那块区域。
[07:18.48]There's also a separate hardware detail: Spyre can fetch a program early, before its patch reaches memory.
[07:18.48]还有一个硬件细节：Spyre 可能在修补数据写入内存前，就提前读取程序。
[07:25.84]A barrier in program distribution holds that fetch until the patch has landed.
[07:25.84]程序分发环节的屏障会让这次读取等到修补数据写入完成。
[07:31.60]Ava: So queue order alone doesn't prevent that early fetch. That's a subtle one.
[07:31.60]Ava：所以光靠队列顺序挡不住提前读取。这个细节挺微妙。
[07:37.52]Brian: It is. The host staging buffer has its own reuse rule.
[07:37.52]Brian：是的。主机暂存缓冲区也有自己的复用规则。
[07:41.20]One preparation stream can reuse it because each transfer finishes reading it before the next callback overwrites it.
[07:41.20]使用单个准备流时可以复用它，因为每次传输都会在下一次回调覆盖缓冲区前读完。
[07:49.16]More preparation streams would need separate buffers or a pool that waits for completion.
[07:49.16]如果有更多准备流，就需要各自的缓冲区，或一个等待传输完成后才复用的缓冲池。
[07:55.56]Ava: You mentioned events. Can a PyTorch user record and wait on Spyre events today?
[07:55.56]Ava：你提到了事件。现在 PyTorch 用户能记录和等待 Spyre 事件吗？
[08:02.37]Brian: The runtime uses software events internally and can derive dependencies when operations' device-memory reads and writes conflict.
[08:02.37]Brian：运行时内部使用软件事件；当操作对设备内存的读写发生冲突时，也能推导出依赖关系。
[08:10.99]User-callable event recording and waiting through PyTorch are planned, but aren't implemented yet.
[08:10.99]计划让用户通过 PyTorch 记录和等待事件，但目前还没实现。
[08:17.55]Users can synchronize a stream or the accelerator to wait for completion.
[08:17.55]用户可以同步单个流或整个加速器，等待操作完成。
[08:22.78]Ava: Let's zoom out. Where does the compiler fit, and why did they remove a runtime graph?
[08:22.78]Ava：回头看整体流程，编译器处于什么位置？他们为什么移除了运行时图？
[08:29.08]Brian: FX graphs, PyTorch's captured computation graphs, stay in Inductor, PyTorch's compiler pipeline.
[08:29.08]Brian：FX 图，也就是 PyTorch 捕获的计算图，保留在 PyTorch 的编译流程 Inductor 中。
[08:36.15]The earlier integration built a second, backend-specific graph after compilation.
[08:36.15]早期集成方案在编译后还会构建一张后端专用图。
[08:42.11]Even a single launch had to read and rebuild graph information around its tensor arguments.
[08:42.11]即使只启动一次，也得围绕张量参数读取并重建图信息。
[08:49.16]Ava: So they prepare the compiled artifact once?
[08:49.16]Ava：所以他们只准备一次编译产物？
[08:52.89]Brian: Yes.
[08:52.89]Brian：对。
[08:53.20]Preparation parses the artifact, allocates and transfers its program binary, and makes an ordered recipe of typed steps.
[08:53.20]准备阶段解析产物，分配并传输程序二进制文件，再生成一份按顺序排列、标明类型的步骤清单。
[09:02.23]Each launch then builds and enqueues the needed host work, transfers, and compute operations.
[09:02.23]每次启动时，再构建并提交所需的主机端任务、数据传输和计算操作。
[09:09.59]Ava: An ordered recipe is easier to picture than another graph.
[09:09.59]Ava：有序的步骤清单比另一张图更容易理解。
[09:13.61]What does that change for eager operations?
[09:13.61]这对即时执行的操作有什么影响？
[09:16.95]Brian: torch-spyre can use the same decomposition in compiled and eager execution.
[09:16.95]Brian：torch-spyre 在编译执行和即时执行中可以使用同一套操作拆解方式。
[09:22.83]Inside a compile trace, PyTorch captures that decomposition in the larger FX graph.
[09:22.83]在编译追踪期间，PyTorch 会把这些拆解后的操作捕获到更大的 FX 图中。
[09:29.35]Outside a trace, the first eager call compiles and caches it; later calls reuse the compiled entry point.
[09:29.35]不在追踪期间时，首次即时调用会编译并缓存它；后续调用则复用编译后的入口。
[09:37.94]Ava: So an eager operation can also test the whole path?
[09:37.94]Ava：所以单个即时执行的操作也能测试整条流程？
[09:41.96]Brian: Right.
[09:41.96]Brian：对。
[09:42.42]Even one operation exercises real tensors, device memory, compilation, and launch.
[09:42.42]即使只有一个操作，也会用到真实张量、设备内存、编译和启动流程。
[09:48.75]If that operation works alone but fails inside a model, the problem is more likely in how operations are combined.
[09:48.75]如果它单独运行正常，却在模型中失败，问题更可能出在操作的组合方式上。
[09:57.91]Ava: What results does the article report?
[09:57.91]Ava：文章报告了哪些结果？
[10:00.85]Brian: On Granite three point three eight B, with batch size one and sequence length one thousand twenty-four, removing graph construction from transfers alone improved prefill by nine point nine percent and decode by thirteen point six percent.
[10:00.85]Brian：在批大小为 1、序列长度为 1024 的 Granite 3.3 8B 上，仅去掉传输环节的图构建，就让预填充提速 9.9%，解码提速 13.6%。
[10:17.02]Ava: And when compute dispatch stopped using that runtime graph too?
[10:17.02]Ava：如果计算调度也不再使用运行时图呢？
[10:21.93]Brian: The reported totals were one point seven times faster prefill and two point four times faster decode.
[10:21.93]Brian：报告的总体结果是预填充速度提高到 1.7 倍，解码速度提高到 2.4 倍。
[10:29.03]Roughly three quarters of the gain came from the compute path.
[10:29.03]约四分之三的性能提升来自计算路径。
[10:33.40]Those numbers describe that model and setup.
[10:33.40]这些数字只针对该模型和测试配置。
[10:36.84]Ava: What still needs work?
[10:36.84]Ava：还有哪些工作要做？
[10:38.97]Brian: First-use eager calls still compile.
[10:38.97]Brian：首次即时调用仍需编译。
[10:41.59]Unsupported operations may fail or fall back, and different tensor sizes may need another compiled artifact.
[10:41.59]不支持的操作可能失败或回退，不同的张量尺寸也可能需要另一个编译产物。
[10:49.46]Native device support doesn't automatically deliver operator coverage, profiling, distributed collectives, or great kernels for every model.
[10:49.46]原生设备支持并不会自动带来全面的算子支持、性能分析、分布式集合通信，或适合每个模型的高效内核。
[11:00.01]Ava: Is there a plan for changing tensor sizes?
[11:00.01]Ava：张量尺寸变化有应对方案吗？
[11:03.55]Brian: The article describes future support for passing actual variable dimension sizes through the same launch-time correction mechanism as addresses.
[11:03.55]Brian：文章提出，未来可通过与地址相同的启动时修补机制，传入可变维度的实际大小。
[11:12.98]Within supported bounds and layout rules, that could let one artifact serve multiple sizes.
[11:12.98]只要符合支持的范围和布局规则，一个产物就可能适用于多种尺寸。
[11:19.28]Ava: Does any of this flow back into PyTorch?
[11:19.28]Ava：这些工作会回馈给 PyTorch 吗？
[11:22.61]Brian: The team contributes to openreg, PyTorch's reference backend for outside devices.
[11:22.61]Brian：团队也为 openreg 做贡献。它是 PyTorch 面向外部设备的参考后端。
[11:28.27]It also tests upstream changes against Spyre through the Cross-Repository CI Relay and plans to contribute reusable tools for adapting upstream tests.
[11:28.27]团队还通过 Cross-Repository CI Relay 在 Spyre 上测试上游改动，并计划贡献可复用的工具，帮助适配上游测试。
[11:39.09]Ava: Okay, three-point recap.
[11:39.09]Ava：好，用三点总结。
[11:41.11]First, Spyre becomes a real PyTorch device, so tensors have managed storage and can stay resident.
[11:41.11]第一，Spyre 成为真正的 PyTorch 设备，张量有了受管理的存储空间，也能常驻设备。
[11:49.71]Brian: Second, compiled artifacts become prepared recipes.
[11:49.71]Brian：第二，编译产物变成预先准备好的步骤清单。
[11:53.80]Launch-time patching supplies tensor addresses, and events order work across streams.
[11:53.80]启动时修补机制填入张量地址，事件则安排跨流任务的执行顺序。
[12:00.98]Ava: Third, that design removes runtime graph work and opens room for transfer and compute overlap, though coverage and public events still need work.
[12:00.98]Ava：第三，这种设计省去了运行时的图处理，也为传输与计算重叠执行创造了条件，不过操作支持范围和公开事件机制仍需完善。
[12:12.06]Brian: That's Spyre's PyTorch story for today. Thanks for listening.
[12:12.06]Brian：以上就是今天 Spyre 与 PyTorch 的故事。感谢收听。
